# 3️⃣ PROBABILITY

Probability measures how likely an event is.

$$
0 \leq P(A) \leq 1
$$

Examples:

```text
P = 0       → impossible
P = 0.5     → 50% chance
P = 1       → certain
```

Example:

A fair coin:

```text
P(Heads) = 1/2
P(Tails) = 1/2
```

---

# Probability in ML

Suppose an email classifier produces:

```text
Spam = 0.92
Not Spam = 0.08
```

The model is essentially saying:

> "Given what I observed, spam has a 92% estimated probability."

This is why probability is everywhere in:

* classification
* Bayesian methods
* Naive Bayes
* logistic regression
* probabilistic models
* generative AI
* language models

