# 1️⃣3️⃣ INTERVIEW PREP 🎯

## Q1. Mean vs Median?

**Answer:**

> Mean is the arithmetic average of all observations, while median is the middle value after sorting. Mean is sensitive to outliers, whereas median is generally more robust to extreme values.

---

## Q2. Why is variance squared?

Important answer:

> Variance squares deviations from the mean so that positive and negative deviations don't cancel each other out. It also mathematically gives a useful measure of dispersion.

---

## Q3. What is standard deviation?

> Standard deviation is the square root of variance and measures the typical spread of observations around the mean in the original units of the data.

---

## Q4. What is bias?

> Bias is the error introduced when a model is too simplistic to capture the underlying pattern, often leading to underfitting.

---

## Q5. What is variance in ML?

Don't confuse statistical variance with model variance.

In ML:

> Model variance refers to how sensitive a model's predictions are to changes in the training dataset.

High model variance often leads to:

```text
Overfitting
```

